{"v":"sugar","rows":[{"cell":"a"}]}
a string: ok -> value: text

an int: ok -> value: 7

a float: ok -> value: 1.5

a big integer: ok -> value: 123456789012345678901

a true: ok -> value: true

a false: ok -> value: false

a decimal: ok -> value: 19.90

null: '@{v}' is bound to null, and it holds a string
an array: '@{v}' is bound to an array, and it holds a string
an object: '@{v}' is bound to an object, and it holds a string
rows from json: ok -> - x
- y

a row that is not an object: '@for .. in rows' needs an array of objects, and element 1 is a number
a for over an object: '@for .. in rows' needs an array, and 'rows' is bound to an object
a context that is an array: a template's context is a JSON object, and this one is an array
a context that is a string: a template's context is a JSON object, and this one is a string
an empty context: '@{v}' is not bound (bound: )
a key nothing uses: 'extra' is bound and template 'one' never mentions it (it uses: v)
